  "original_name": "Casseta & Planeta, Urgente!",
  "overview": "Casseta & Planeta is a Brazilian group of comedians who run a TV show named Casseta & Planeta Urgente, broadcast by Rede Globo. The humour featured on the show is mostly satirical, relating to religious or ethical groups, and minorities.\n\nThe group founded a company called Toviassu Produções Artísticas, whose name is an acronym composed of syllables from the phrase \"Todo viado é surdo\" – \"Every gay is deaf\"; which is the ending of a widely known Brazilian practical joke. Each one of the seven members has a specific function within the company. They present their TV show at Rede Globo and publish a website and many books, among other products, for example the \"Machobol\".\n\nOriginally a magazine named Casseta Popular and a humour newspaper called O Planeta Diário, the two teams joined forces and were hired by Rede Globo to become writers for the network's comedy shows, starting with TV Pirata in 1988. A few years later, they starred in their own show.",
